{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-5543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $n\\ge 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-2)!}{n!}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-5543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\nn!=n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-2)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-2)!}{n!} & =\\frac{(n-2)!}{n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(n-2)!}}{n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot \\cancel{(n-2)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-5543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "398c86a0025cca31068b41f9c6a501cb802fc557f2efc48fc909357ff4c9215c"} {"question" "q-5543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-5543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(n-1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{n}"] ["math" "\\frac{n}{(n-1)}"] ["math" "n(n-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-5543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-6398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $k\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{{k}^{2}(k-1)!}{(k+1)k!}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-6398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that\n\n$$\nk!=k(k-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $k(k-1)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{k}^{2}(k-1)!}{(k+1)k!} & =\\frac{k\\cdot k(k-1)!}{(k+1)\\cdot k(k-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{k\\cdot \\cancel{k(k-1)!}}{(k+1)\\cdot \\cancel{k(k-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{k+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-6398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "398c86a0025cca31068b41f9c6a501cb802fc557f2efc48fc909357ff4c9215c"} {"question" "q-6398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-6398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{k-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{k}{k+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{k}{k-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{k}{{k}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "{k}^{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-6398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{k}{k+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $m\\ge 1$ is an integer, $\\frac{(m!)^{2}}{(m+1)!\\,(m-1)!}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+1)! & =(m+1)\\cdot m! \\\\ m! & =m\\cdot (m-1)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $m!$ and $(m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(m!)^{2}}{(m+1)!\\,(m-1)!} & =\\frac{m!\\cdot m!}{(m+1)!\\,(m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{m!\\cdot m\\cdot (m-1)!}{(m+1)\\cdot m!\\cdot (m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{m!}\\cdot m\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}}{(m+1)\\cdot \\cancel{m!}\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{m}{m+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "398c86a0025cca31068b41f9c6a501cb802fc557f2efc48fc909357ff4c9215c"} {"question" "q-19885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(m+1)^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{m+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{m}^{2}-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{m}{m+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{{m}^{2}}{{m}^{2}-1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{m}{m+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $m\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(2m)!\\,(m+4)!}{(m+5)!\\,(2m-1)!}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+5)! & =(m+5)(m+4)! \\\\ 2m! & =2m(2m-1)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $(m+4)!$ and $(2m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2m)!\\,(m+4)!}{(m+5)!\\,(2m-1)!} & =\\frac{(2m)\\,\\cdot (2m-1)!\\cdot (m+4)!}{(m+5)\\cdot (m+4)!\\cdot (2m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2m)\\,\\cdot \\cancel{(2m-1)!}\\cdot \\cancel{(m+4)!}}{(m+5)\\cdot \\cancel{(m+4)!}\\cdot \\cancel{(2m-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2m}{m+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "398c86a0025cca31068b41f9c6a501cb802fc557f2efc48fc909357ff4c9215c"} {"question" "q-19887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2m"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{m+5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2m}{m+4}"] ["math" "\\frac{2m}{m+5}"] ["math" "\\frac{m}{m+4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-19887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2m}{m+5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-122047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $n\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-1)!}{(n+2)!}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-122047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(n+2)!=(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-1)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-1)!}{(n+2)!} & =\\frac{(n-1)!}{(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(n-1)!}}{(n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot \\cancel{(n-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n(n+1)(n+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-122047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "398c86a0025cca31068b41f9c6a501cb802fc557f2efc48fc909357ff4c9215c"} {"question" "q-122047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981131/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9ad0685d59dc57b55e206c96c3940078bd779cdfe74123d97b026f42cb212ad"} {"question" "q-122047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{(n+1)(n+2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{n(n+1)(n+2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{n(n+1)}"] ["math" "